 * Register a set of definitions under a normalized `/{version}` path
 * prefix and tag every resulting link with that API version.
 *
 *     return [
 *         ...Link::prefix('/api')->group(fn () => [
 *             ...Link::version('v1', fn () => [
 *                 Link::get('/users', [UserController::class, 'index']),
 *             ]),
 *             ...Link::version('v2', fn () => [
 *                 Link::get('/users', [V2\UserController::class, 'index']),
 *             ]),
 *         ]),
 *     ];
 *
 * Version tags survive prefix/group rebasing ({@see Router::rebase()}),
 * so the final routes report `/api/v1/...` paths and `apiVersion() v1`.
 * Nesting a version group inside another version group — `/v1/v2` or
 * `/v1/v1` — is an error, never a silent double prefix.
 *
 * @param string $version identifier; `'v1'`, `'V2'`, `'1'`, `'v2.5'` normalize to `vN`
 * @param Closure(): (Link|list<Link>) $definition
